{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788112573103168777,"compiled_state":{"alias":"byzantine-spinelike-penguin","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"66636ea95dbe688ecbaf5fb0c9ba629e6d1645ebf4cc78ff82516e565e01b00d","event_uuid":"0c1b7f70-7172-42e3-aa59-74951376f0e8","position":{"commit_sha":"cc08ce49f0bc26dcfb53514c4850caf60eea87d4","position":"1788112435373314417-0c1b7f70-7172-42e3-aa59-74951376f0e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ddb9dd88d6764f8ab9bb1fd96337fb6eeb9dba567ed342101406e3f7652cd44d","event_uuid":"f379a6e5-22ef-477c-aaad-deb1d0fb5ebc","position":{"commit_sha":"31f29f9329c62dd17a02aab03d4d1d37f981bd13","position":"1788112573103168776-f379a6e5-22ef-477c-aaad-deb1d0fb5ebc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788112435373314417,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f379a6e5-22ef-477c-aaad-deb1d0fb5ebc","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fc84-a6a6-14c3-4bc8"}],"description":"## Problem\nOnce aggregation, review-bot/CLI rendering, and the workflow gate no longer read `severity`\n(prior sibling tickets), the field itself should be removed from the finding shape per the\nADR decision -- `findings.py`'s `SEVERITIES` vocabulary, `normalize_finding`'s\nclamp-to-\"info\" behavior, the `Finding.severity` Pydantic field, `common.schema.json`'s\n`$defs/finding.severity` (a REQUIRED field there, referenced by `completion_verdict.schema.json`\nand `review_result.schema.json` -- this is the one documented BREAKING schema change), and the\nnow-fully-vestigial `BLOCKING_SEVERITIES`/`blocking_severities` config in\n`review_bot/config.py` (already unused in the current `code_review_decision` flow per\n`adapter.py`'s own docstring).\n\n## Approach\n1. Remove `severity` from `pass3_decide`'s emitted finding dict (`review_kernel/decide.py`) --\n   keep `severity_label()` itself as an internal impact-bucketing helper (still used by\n   calibration/eval code and `test_divergence_grade_split.py`), just stop stamping its output\n   into the finding.\n2. Remove `SEVERITIES`, the severity clamp in `normalize_finding`, and the `Finding.severity`\n   Pydantic field from `findings.py`.\n3. Make `severity` non-required then remove it from `common.schema.json`'s `$defs/finding`\n   (delete the `$defs/severity` def once nothing references it).\n4. Remove `DEFAULT_BLOCKING_SEVERITIES`/`blocking_severities` from `review_bot/config.py` and\n   its env-var registration.\n5. Add the one required BREAKING entry to `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`\n   documenting the `finding.severity` field removal from `completion_verdict` and\n   `review_result`, per `docs/api-stability.md`'s policy for required-field removal.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `grep -rn '\"severity\"' src/rebar/llm/findings.py src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/decide.py`\n  finds no finding-shape references (historical comments/docstrings are acceptable).\n- [ ] `common.schema.json`'s `$defs/finding.required` no longer lists `severity`.\n- [ ] `review_bot/config.py` has no `blocking_severities`/`BLOCKING_SEVERITIES` symbol; the\n  matching tests in `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py` and `tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py`\n  are removed or updated to assert the symbol's absence.\n- [ ] `docs/release-notes.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` each have a new BREAKING entry naming the\n  `finding.severity` removal from `completion_verdict`/`review_result`.\n- [ ] `make test` passes with the full suite -- no remaining test constructs a finding via\n  `severity=` and expects it to round-trip.\n\n## Testing\nTier: in-process unit tests (schema validation against a finding dict with no `severity` key\npasses `common.schema.json`'s finding validator) plus a contract test (`pass3_decide`'s real\noutput fed to the schema validator). Oracle: schema validation succeeds without `severity`;\n`severity_label()` remains importable and correct for its retained calibration/eval callers --\nexisting `test_severity_label_buckets`/`test_divergence_grade_split.py` tests keep passing\nunchanged, proving the helper's own behavior is untouched even though it is decoupled from\nthe Finding shape.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","fc84-a6a6-14c3-4bc8"],["parent","c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"c4c8-317a-85ca-4b08","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"029d-126b-d781-42f7","ticket_type":"task","title":"Drop the severity field from the finding shape (BREAKING)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0c1b7f70-7172-42e3-aa59-74951376f0e8","f379a6e5-22ef-477c-aaad-deb1d0fb5ebc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788112573103168777,"uuid":"754fe963-1acf-489c-8496-db508b2f1bef"}